        "original_id": "20fb5536-8331-5804-8da6-f0f0e8dd7a50",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Water dropwort, Costus\n- Taxa: Oenanthe, Apiaceae, Costaceae\n- Compounds: Oenanthotoxin\n- Species: Oenanthe crocata\n- People: Linnaeus\n\nFacts:\n- In 1753, Linnaeus described Costus as a genus.\n- Costus is a group of perennial herbaceous plants in the family Costaceae.\n- Water dropworts are plants in the genus Oenanthe.\n- Oenanthe is a genus in the family Apiaceae.\n- Oenanthotoxin is a toxin extracted from Oenanthe crocata and other plants of the genus Oenanthe.",
